How can I use PHP to assign Scrabble point values to the letters in the words "Queen", "Knight", and "Rook" using the standard point system? And how can I arrange these words in descending order based on their total point values, taking into account any bonus points for using all seven letters in a single turn?
Here is the PHP code I am currently using:
$scrabblePoints = array(
    "A" => 1, "B" => 3, "C" => 3, "D" => 2,
    "E" => 1, "F" => 4, "G" => 2, "H" => 4,
    "I" => 1, "J" => 8, "K" => 5, "L" => 1,
    "M" => 3, "N" => 1, "O" => 1, "P" => 3,
    "Q" => 10, "R" => 1, "S" => 1, "T" => 1,
    "U" => 1, "V" => 4, "W" => 4, "X" => 8,
    "Y" => 4, "Z" => 10
);
$words = array("Queen", "Knight", "Rook");
$totalPoints = array();
foreach ($words as $word) {
    $points = 0;
    $letters = str_split($word);
    foreach ($letters as $letter) {
        $points += $scrabblePoints[strtoupper($letter)];
    }
    if (count($letters) == 7) {
        $points += 50; // add bonus points for using all 7 letters
    }
    $totalPoints[$word] = $points;
}
arsort($totalPoints);
echo "Words in descending order of their total point value: <br>";
foreach ($totalPoints as $word => $points) {
    echo $word . ": " . $points . "<br>";
}

